invariant: INV-5
file: webpki_name.c
catches: webpki_name_test
reason: admitting '*' into the reference-name alphabet lets a caller's
  "*.example.test" pass webpki_hostname_ok, the check docs/webpki.md
  calls the whole defence against a presented name carrying NUL or '*':
  the matcher compares equal-length byte ranges against the reference
  name and refuses nothing itself, so the shape check has its own
  mutant. bin/webpki_name_test's alphabet rows object.

--- old
    return is_letter(c) || is_digit(c) || c == '.' || c == '-';
--- new
    return is_letter(c) || is_digit(c) || c == '.' || c == '-' || c == '*';
